[L3_VERBATIM]
name: implement_utc_standardized_i18n_infrastructure
description: Establishing a unified backend UTC-only time standard paired with a localized frontend for language and timezone-aware user interfaces.
goal: Achieve data integrity across distributed systems by enforcing UTC internally while providing localized user experiences.
inputs:
  - Backend data models and pipelines
  - Frontend UI architecture
  - Supported locale/language list
  - User timezone detection mechanism
use_when: When scaling an application to support multiple geographic regions or languages.
payload:
  - Modify backend models and data pipelines to enforce UTC for all datetime storage and processing.
  - Update backend serializers/deserializers to ensure all incoming and outgoing timestamps are treated as UTC.
  - Implement an i18n framework on the frontend to replace hardcoded strings with localized, state-driven variables.
  - Add a language selection UI to allow users to switch between supported locales.
  - Implement frontend logic to detect the user's local timezone and dynamically format UTC timestamps into a human-readable local format.
[/L3_VERBATIM]